From 022ef6a9caabddc398e83a3afd4dd7acf55d0c9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:17:31 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Texture dump: a menu option, and every key a pack needs

Dumping textures to start a pack was only <prefix>_TEXTURE_DUMP, read at
start. The Video page's texture pack rows now have Dump textures: on, it
writes into textures/dump/<disc id> in the data directory (or the
variable's folder) and drops the texture cache so those already loaded
are written too; off, it waits for the queued images. It is not saved,
so a dump left on cannot fill the disk unnoticed; the footer says how
many images it has written.

Two textures a pack needs were never dumped:
- A 512-tall texture is hashed again over more rows when it is drawn
  further down, and finds another key; only a pack being loaded did
  that, and the dump only wrote at upload. With a dump on, it is hashed
  again too and written under the new key (decoded once more).
- The dumper marked a texture written before dropping it for a full
  queue, so it was never written. It now checks the queue first.

Checked with Dissidia 012 on Windows (llvm-mingw build): the title
screen's 512x512 atlas was dumped under both its keys (it had one); a
pack made from the dump alone, with those two images four times the
size, replaced the title screen to its menu; the menu option, turned on
at the title screen, wrote both keys, showed "2 images written", and
turned off. The 21 framework tests pass (MSVC, ad hoc excluded) and
portablekit_host_check builds. Not tried: a whole game's dump, the
queue-full case, Linux.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
